//! msvcrt.dll — Microsoft Visual C Runtime
//!
//! Provides the C runtime library functions (printf, malloc, strcpy, etc.)
//! for programs compiled with MSVC. This is a complete implementation
//! of the C runtime library for NT6.1 (Windows 7).
//!
//! Clean-room implementation. Spec source: MSVCRT documentation,
//! Microsoft Visual Studio headers, ISO C99/C11 standards.
//!
//! ## Modules
//! - **types**: C types and structures (FILE, tm, errno_t, etc.)
//! - **memory**: Memory management (malloc, free, calloc, realloc, aligned allocations)
//! - **string**: String operations (strcpy, strcmp, strlen, memcpy, memset)
//! - **stdio**: File and formatted I/O (fopen, fread, fwrite, printf, sprintf)
//! - **math**: Mathematical functions (sin, cos, sqrt, pow, log, exp)
//! - **wchar**: Wide character support (wcslen, wcscpy, mbstowcs, wcstombs)
//! - **time**: Time and date functions (time, clock, localtime, gmtime, strftime)
//! - **convert**: String conversion and character classification (atoi, strtol, itoa, isalpha, isdigit)
//! - **process**: Process control (exit, abort, atexit, getenv, system)
//!
//! ## Integration with NT6.1 Kernel
//! - Memory operations integrate with kernel memory manager (mm)
//! - File I/O integrates with kernel I/O subsystem (io)
//! - Uses kernel RTL (runtime library) utilities where appropriate
//!
//! ## Standards Compliance
//! - ISO C99 standard library functions
//! - Microsoft Visual C++ runtime extensions
//! - Windows-specific CRT functions (_aligned_malloc, _itoa_s, etc.)

